  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing Women&apos;s Rights in Konso:  Elevating Grassroots Associations to Champion Social Change and Policy Advocacy.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen the capacity and operational space of women&#x2019;s associations and advocacy groups in the target area so they can effectively promote women&#x2019;s rights, challenge harmful social norms, and participate meaningfully in local governance. It will provide tailored leadership and advocacy training to 300 women leaders, including rural women, to enhance their ability to engage in policy dialogue. The project will also establish and reinforce functional rural women&#x2019;s advocacy groups with improved networking and collaborative skills. Additionally, it will facilitate community dialogues and sustained campaigns to address harmful practices, particularly early marriage, leading to increased reporting and reduced cases in the targeted districts by the project&#x2019;s end.</narrative>
  </description>
